@startuml
title Coding Agent 1.2.0 - Static validation selection and dispatch
start
:Inspect changed paths and text shebangs;
if (Bash shebang or .sh without POSIX sh shebang?) then (yes)
  :Recommend bash_syntax, then shellcheck;
elseif (POSIX sh shebang?) then (yes)
  :Recommend shellcheck only;
elseif (Recognized playbook or file inside an Ansible role?) then (yes)
  :Use playbook path or owning role directory;
  :Recommend ansible_syntax, then ansible_lint;
else (unrelated file)
  :No automatic static recommendation;
  stop
endif
:Receive semantic run_check name + relative targets;
if (Secure target validation succeeds?) then (no)
  :Return INVALID_TARGET without execution;
  stop
else (yes)
  if (Trusted checker installed?) then (no)
    :Return SKIPPED; never install dependencies;
    stop
  else (yes)
    :Build fixed argv; role syntax uses private wrapper;
    :Execute through SandboxRunner in a fresh snapshot;
    :Preserve diagnostics and exact check status;
    note right
      bash -n and Ansible syntax: separate runs per target
      ShellCheck: one process for validated files, no -x
      Ansible: synthetic inventory, controlled config, offline lint
      SKIPPED and SANDBOX_ERROR never mean PASS
      Static results do not prove runtime or converge correctness
    end note
  endif
endif
stop
@enduml
